@startuml learning-data-sharing
!include _standard-style.puml

title Sharing learned data across a team — git is the only transport

actor "Alice" as A
participant "Alice's obs-api\n(owns her store)" as OA
participant "X/.coding\n(Alice)" as CA
database "bmw.ghe.com\nX-history" as R
participant "X/.coding\n(Bob)" as CB
participant "Bob's obs-api" as OB
actor "Bob's agent" as B

== Alice learns ==
A -> OA : session in X → observations,\ndigests, insights, KB entities
OA -> CA : export kb/knowledge-graph/X.json\n(canonical order; unchanged file = not rewritten)
note over CA
  LSL transcripts land in history/ directly
  (the session logger writes through the symlink).
end note
CA -> CA : local commit — at session end\nand every 30 min (health coordinator)
A -> CA : ""coding sync --push"" (asks first)
CA -> R : git push

== Bob picks it up ==
B -> CB : next ""coding"" launch in X\n(or ""coding sync pull"")
CB -> R : git pull
R --> CB : Alice's commits
note over CB
  Both changed X.json? The registered git merge
  driver (lib/kb/merge-driver.mjs) merges the graph
  with the hydrate rule — no text conflicts.
end note
CB -> OB : POST /api/kb/reload
OB -> OB : union merge into the live store\nnewest updatedAt wins · relations by (from,type,to)\ntombstones delete everywhere (90 days)
OB -> OB : embed backfill — only what arrived;\nprune points of tombstoned entities
B -> OB : prompt → /api/retrieve\n(filtered to X's teams)
OB --> B : Alice's insight injected

== Teammates without a checkout of X ==
note over CB, OB
  A ""repos:"" entry that is only a remote (Alice's X-history)
  is cloned under &#126;/.coding/data/<scope>/var/shared/X/ —
  pull-only, merged into the store, never written.
end note

@enduml
